    "pressure": {
      "file": "condensate_recovery_system_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Recover heat, water and chemicals",
      "description": "High-pressure condensate entering a lower pressure partly flashes to steam: flash fraction = (h_f,high − h_f,low) / h_fg,low (≈ 10–15 % from ~10 bar to atmosphere). The flash vessel sends this steam to the LP header; the remaining hot condensate (already treated water, ≈ 90–100 °C) returns to the boiler, saving fuel, make-up water and treatment chemicals. Pumps handling near-boiling water need generous NPSH, which is why the receiver is raised above them.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
